From 97345f8b98897afb3b56267c7048537ea4845ba5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stevedamnvan <100538383+stevedamnvan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:16:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] cast-ps2-25: GC-ASSET credits the PS2 Ashley's masked runs to
 her package (allowlist 93 -> 87)

The 6 "GameCube cast model still drawn" rows em/pl01.drs#body (17c2d1a1, 9d447531, ddfc4b21) in r11e and r11f
were a census misattribution, not a GameCube draw. The bytes are GC pl11 BINs 7 / 6 / 9 (head, hair, skirt;
byte-identical in pl01.drs, hence the label). The partner Ashley is fully drawn by her PS2 registry package
(ash21/ashley11: NMRS plan=R every frame). But her head, hair and skirt sections are masked sections: two runs
that use the section's positions with the UV and stream of mask_geometry[0] / [1]. gcasset_actor_current_select
matched only whole chunk views, found none and accepted the run on the source info's GC member.
Diagnostic twin (7250e5c6): posmatch=1 uvmatch=0 streammatch=0 for exactly those three infos.

Fix (GC_ASSET_GATE builds only; the .inc is inside #if RE4DC_GC_ASSET_GATE): also match a masked section's
run views, with every consumed array inside the same package proof.

Gates: gate-ON census on cand-2e8a7cef + this tree (catalog cat15 edc56207): r11e and r11f kind=model rows 0
(control 3 each). The other rows are unchanged allowed unknown textures. The judge's remaining failures are the
pre-existing motion-unknown-accepted-records / payload-catalog-bind errors, also present in the control.
Release image unchanged: route-build of the rr recipe from this tree = 57a3450d957641d2 (rr cand-2e8a7cef).
So KOS, heap 4 and gameplay are untouched and there is no look change.
Evidence C:\Flycast-Evidence\re4-dreamcast\cast-ps2-25 (cg-r11e-j, cg-r11f-j; diag cg-r11e-d5).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AkGpf8W8oYKd2z6cLgVseU
---
 .../include/gc_asset_actor_select.inc         | 17 ++++++
 .../tools/d367/gc_port23/allowlist.json       | 60 -------------------
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 60 deletions(-)

diff --git a/port/dreamcast/game/platform/include/gc_asset_actor_select.inc b/port/dreamcast/game/platform/include/gc_asset_actor_select.inc
index 1dce3bd94..34432fa03 100644
--- a/port/dreamcast/game/platform/include/gc_asset_actor_select.inc
+++ b/port/dreamcast/game/platform/include/gc_asset_actor_select.inc
@@ -86,6 +86,23 @@ re4dc_gcasset::SourceUse gcasset_actor_current_select(const Re4dcModelPart* part
         if(gcasset_actor_chunk(c,c.uv_bytes,*part,*source))
             for(auto& proof:gcasset_registry)if(gcasset_actor_bound(proof,c,c.uv_bytes))accept(proof);
     }
+#if RE4DC_NMR_MASK
+    // cast-ps2-25: a masked section draws two runs (coarse_actor_owner_registry.inc plan): the section's own
+    // positions / normals / palettes with the UV + stream of its run geometry mask_geometry[0] (opaque) or [1]
+    // (alpha-masked cards: the PS2 Ashley's head, hair and skirt). Without this the run matched no view and was
+    // reported as the GameCube member of its source info (pl11 BINs 6 / 7 / 9), though the PS2 package drew it.
+    // Every consumed array must still lie inside the same package proof.
+    for(unsigned k=0;k<registry.chunk_count;++k){
+        const auto& s=registry.chunks[k];
+        for(unsigned h=0;h<2;++h){
+            if(s.mask_geometry[h]==~0u || s.mask_geometry[h]>=registry.geometry_count)continue;
+            const auto base=registry_gview(s.geometry),run=registry_gview(s.mask_geometry[h]);
+            auto c=base;c.uv=run.uv;c.uv_bytes=run.uv_bytes;c.stream=run.stream;c.stream_bytes=run.stream_bytes;
+            if(gcasset_actor_chunk(c,c.uv_bytes,*part,*source))
+                for(auto& proof:gcasset_registry)if(gcasset_actor_bound(proof,c,c.uv_bytes))accept(proof);
+        }
+    }
+#endif
 #endif
 #if RE4DC_ACTOR_PL08 && RE4DC_ACTOR_PL08_PACK
     if(pl08_pack.published)for(unsigned k=0;k<3;++k){const auto& c=pl08_pack_chunks[k];const unsigned uv_bytes=pl08_pack.view[k].bytes[2];
